                <note rend="inline" type="source">875.6363/161: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Albania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kodding</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tirana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-11T19:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 11,
                                1925—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 12—9:20
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>16. Legation’s 13, February 7 [<hi rendition="#italic">8</hi>], 8 p.m.<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d338-f1"/> The Minister for Foreign Affairs stated upon being
                    pressed this morning that the Constituent Assembly would possibly remain in
                    session for about 20 days more and if so the granting of the oil concession
                    would be considered although, according to the Foreign Office, the Cabinet has
                    not yet acted upon the question. The British Minister is said to be exerting
                    pressure in his almost daily conferences with the Ministers. One of the two
                    projects mentioned in my 15, February 10, 9 a.m. is admitted by the Ministry to
                    be banking concession to British representatives who are now in Tirana. He was
                    noncommittal concerning the second. Situation is very acute.</p>
                <p>Copy to European Information Center.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kodding</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
